  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-04, branch jgstern-agent/fix/mahik (worktree ~/hg_wt/mahik), commit a9ed664683, NOT pushed. No status change.\n\nPremise re-verified on origin/dev 385ec63be1 (both halves reproduced; fixture in the commit's test).\n\nFix (perl.py): a bareword invocant (Pkg, Pkg::, ::Pkg) or __PACKAGE__ is looked up as Pkg::m exactly (main -> bare m). A miss emits perl:<Pkg>:0-0:<m>:unresolved with dst_ref module_path=Pkg, which is the function arm's spelling for LWP::Simple::get (one shared helper now). Both carry call_construct=function (ADR-0059). Class-method calls outside a sub are attributed to the file. Expression invocants are unchanged. Spec line on top-level anchoring corrected.\n\nTests: test_perl_class_method.py. Red on origin/dev: 11 failed, 4 passed. Green, targeted smart-test, 297 files: 9795 passed, 2 xfailed, 0 failed; perl.py at 100% coverage.\n\nBehaviour (verify-claims, overlay fs_read module IO::File functions [new], claim must_not_exist): IO::File->new is confirmed on origin/dev (a false all-clear: the call bound the repo's Local::new) and violated on the branch. Controls: Local->new stays confirmed; Other::File->new gives inconclusive. A mutant that drops the package from the module slot turns Other::File violated, so that control can fail.\n\nMeasured by call site, analyze_perl on frozen perl-file copies (~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_10032026/mahik/):\n- No edge changed outside a class-method site in any repo.\n- Bindings to ANOTHER package's sub: 173 to 0.\n- Bindings to the invocant's own sub: 48 to 769 (postgresql 399 of them top-level TAP calls).\n- External package sites: 0 to 204.\n- Per repo: git 98 sites, postgresql 441, virtualbox 423, ceph 2, kong 10.\n- Inherited-call losses: 3 sites lost an in-repo binding; all 3 were wrong bindings.\n- Default-config verify-claims on the git/postgresql perl files is unchanged: inconclusive in both arms, because perl has no I/O catalogue.\n\nResiduals filed:\n- WI-mugir-tupuj-tiras-diror-kutis-dusup-tatuv-rikat (P2): expression invocants.\n- WI-jubuk-rufus-tonab-kifiv-madom-pipaf-dofis-putam (P3): no perl inheritance.\n- WI-lomon-hapul-tudub-buvog-pazaz-hibut-latak-zokiz (P3): no perl I/O catalogue.\nNote posted on WI-jadaf."  # a0fe
